The host executable uses the production speech_tts_speak, engine and converter.
Its only hardware substitution is audio_playback_write_checked. It checks
nonzero samples, stereo duplication, bounded writes, propagated output failure
and recovery. Separate process output comparison checks deterministic waveform
with the fixed random seed. ffplay is optional, not a build dependency.

Native Codex subscription voice (experimental provider compatibility)
------------------------------------------------------------------
The local eSpeak pipeline above is retained unchanged. The optional Codex path
is native WebRTC Opus plus an authenticated provider sideband, not LAN bridge
PCM, paid API speech, paid STT, or a local fallback. No account/setup HTTP route
starts capture. Read-aloud has no microphone task, reads only an already quoted
8192-byte passage, requires canonical assistant turn.done plus audible/drained
playback, and is bounded to 125 seconds after readiness and 150 seconds decoded
audio. Stop is latched before queued read-aloud/authentication starts.

Protocol facts were inspected against OpenAI Codex commit
72f999edc7848961b99c4b98bf1e62d12fa35798, particularly
codex-api/src/endpoint/realtime_call.rs and realtime_websocket/
protocol_frameless_bidi.rs and methods_frameless_bidi.rs. OpenAI Codex is
Apache-2.0, Copyright 2025 OpenAI; upstream LICENSE and NOTICE are at
https://github.com/openai/codex/tree/72f999edc7848961b99c4b98bf1e62d12fa35798.
The session uses gpt-live-1-codex with client delegation, the ChatGPT backend
realtime/calls quicksilver/avas JSON shape, Codex Desktop 0.159.0 headers, and
wss://api.openai.com/v1/live/<validated-call-id>. Subscription eligibility and
future undocumented-provider compatibility remain provider/hardware gates.
Context text is split on UTF-8 boundaries into <=500-byte input_text chunks.
Mirrored event/item identities and independent ordered-source turn ordinals
deduplicate delivery without merging identical text in later turns.

