Only specific esp_opus_enc_open/get_frame_size/process/reset/close and
esp_opus_dec_open/decode/close APIs are linked by the adapter; no all-codec
registry. PCM is native 16000 Hz stereo PCM16, Opus frames are 20 ms on capture;
SDP and RTP scaling remain standard opus/48000/2. esp_peer_open/new_connection/
send_msg/main_loop/send_audio/create_data_channel/close provide ICE, DTLS-SRTP
and SCTP. Google STUN (stun.l.google.com:19302) gathers public ICE candidates;
it cannot authorize the peer. Locally created oai-events is explicitly reliable
and ordered, with manual_ch_create=true, and automatic reconnect is disabled.

Peer identity security is enforced, not inferred from encrypted media.
The shipped SDK DTLS source accepts optional PKI verification and does not bind
the certificate to SDP. The component linker wraps dtls_srtp_handshake; the S3
archive has an external R_XTENSA_32 relocation to that symbol in
peer_on_connecting's literal pool (offset 0x2c), and an R_XTENSA_ASM_EXPAND call
relocation at offset 0x06. The wrapper compares the actual peer leaf DER SHA-256
with the fingerprint from the verified-HTTPS answer before returning success
to the peer state machine. Missing/conflicting/non-SHA-256 fingerprints and
mismatching/missing certificates fail closed with a fixed credential-free error.
The negotiated SRTP profile must also be authenticated AES128_CM_HMAC_SHA1
(80- or 32-bit tag); the SDK's advertised NULL-encryption profiles are rejected.
The only private ABI member read is dtls_srtp_t.ssl; shipped S3 DWARF places it
at offset 8, guarded at compile time together with 32-bit S3/IDF5-6 constraints.
Retain CONFIG_MBEDTLS_SSL_KEEP_PEER_CERTIFICATE, DTLS and DTLS-SRTP. Re-audit
the hook, ELF call target and ABI on SDK/target upgrades. The native-only
speech_live_peer_security_smoke signaling-callback seam exercises the production
esp_peer task/answer parser/real handshake, never mic or credentials. Its negative
mode corrupts only the expected digest and must return the fixed fingerprint
failure after a real handshake; a direct unit call to the wrapper is not proof.

HTTPS uses the certificate bundle and hostname verification, no redirects.
The sideband reuses the hardened TLS WebSocket parser, requiring a verified
api.openai.com TLS connection and a checked HTTP 101/Sec-WebSocket-Accept, with
no extension negotiation or binary audio. esp_websocket_client 1.8.0 was
inspected but is not used here: it follows 3xx redirects on IDF>=5.5.1 without
a disable-redirect configuration. Ready requires both the verified peer/
oai-events channel and session.started/updated on the authenticated sideband.
The adapter logs no tokens, remote errors, SDP, peer addresses or provider bodies.
SDK transport diagnostics may log ICE addresses; these are not account tokens.

Runtime bounds (SDK/JSON/codec allocator overhead additional):
- Four internal-stack tasks at priority 5: control 8192 bytes, peer 8192,
  capture 4096 (conversation only), playback 4096. All media/peer tasks join
  before TLS/queue/context destruction and the terminal closed callback.
- PSRAM fixed packet pools: 8 Tx slots (<=1275 encoded bytes each) and 16 Rx
  slots (<=7650 bytes each, <=120 ms Opus); ready/free queues transfer pointers.
  Encoder writes straight into pooled Tx packets; Rx payload is copied once
  from SDK-owned memory, decoded directly, and PCM is written without copies.
  Shared fixed PCM scratch is 1280 capture plus 7680 decoder bytes.
- Four provider-event slots, each <=65536 bytes in PSRAM; four context slots,
  each <=16384 bytes plus the delegation prefix; one 65537-byte control scratch,
  two 16385-byte SDP buffers, and bounded PSRAM transcript/identity storage.
  Media pressure is bounded to 2 seconds; event/context pressure ends the call
  rather than dropping finalized transcripts or growing queues.
- SDK data caches: 8192 send / 69632 receive bytes; audio jitter 32768 bytes/
  100 ms; RTP send pool 16384 bytes/16 metadata slots/two resend attempts.
  Eight gathered ICE candidates; authenticated answer accepts <=16 candidates,
  <=16384 SDP bytes, <=1024 bytes/line, and only matching SHA-256 fingerprints.
- Transcript text <=8192 bytes, JSON nesting <=16, 128 recent stable event
  identities, 64 delegation identities / four pending delegations.
  Muting increments capture generation, clears queued packet ownership, resets
  encoder state on the next generation and gates the peer hand-off boundary.
  Already handed-off RTP cannot be revoked. RMS echo gating is not AEC.

Build, real mismatched-certificate handshake rejection, account signaling,
ICE/NAT compatibility, sustained duplex Opus/codec playback, mute and Stop
timing must be verified on the final integrated S3 firmware; no such hardware
or provider result is implied by these source/SDK observations.
